From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:23:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(loss): opt-in dump of the tokens where generation and
 trainer logprobs disagree

token_mult_prob_error is a token mean of exp(|generation - prev|), so a
handful of tokens with a gap of 10+ nats dominate it, and the metric does
not say which tokens they are. Job 5304373 (Apertus 2 SFT checkpoint, FP8
vLLM, Megatron trainer): 1.03 at step 1, before any refit, then 6.97 and
26.54, max_seq_mult_prob_error 390, while gen_kl_error stays ~0.0025, i.e.
a few tokens with generation logprob >> trainer logprob.

With NRL_LOGPROB_DUMP_DIR set in the policy workers' environment (for
Megatron: policy.megatron_cfg.env_vars), ClippedPGLossFn appends JSON
lines per loss call to <dir>/logprob-<host>-<pid>.jsonl: a call record
(rows, valid tokens, tokens over 1/2/5/10 nats, every row's
seq_mult_prob_error) and, for rows whose largest gap reaches
NRL_LOGPROB_DUMP_MIN_NATS (default 3), a seq record plus up to
NRL_LOGPROB_DUMP_MAX_TOKENS (default 32) token records, worst first: token
id, position, generation/prev/current logprob, advantage, which generated
burst it is in and its offset there, neighbouring token ids and logprobs.
A seq_key hash of the token ids joins records across ranks. Tensor
parallel ranks other than 0 write nothing.

Unset, the hook is one environment lookup. Failures are logged once and
never raised.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
